// Data of the theorem graph (theorems.html): theorems, lemmas, corollaries and conjectures of geometry, MSC 2020 51
// (foundations, Euclidean, projective and hyperbolic geometry), 52A (convexity) and 53 (differential geometry). In
// English. Built on 3 November 2026; no theorem with first class 51, 52A or 53 existed in the other folders.
//
// Model as in ../../algebraic-number-theory/data/theorem-graph.js (see its header comment): `premises` and `proof` are
// the standard textbook proof, named in `proofName`; further proofs in `alternativeProofs`; `foundation: true` marks
// theorems whose proof rests on theory outside these graphs. `area` is the three-character class as in
// data/concepts.js. `concepts` are ids of data/concepts.js or carry the prefix of another folder.
// Elementary Euclidean geometry follows Euclid's Elements in Hilbert's axiomatic form (Hartshorne, Geometry: Euclid and
// Beyond): a theorem proved from Hilbert's axioms and definitions alone carries `fromDefinitions`. Premises list only
// theorems that are not already premises of another listed premise (tests/check-theorems.js warns otherwise).
// References to theorems of other folders: "gt:", "ar:" (Galois theory, finite fields), "ant:" (cyclotomic fields),
// "co:" (spectral theorem, Euler's polyhedron formula), "rt:" (bases and dimension), "ag:" (Bézout), and the new
// folders "ana:" and "top:" with the ids listed in the report.
//
// Sources: Euclid, Elements (Heath's edition, 1908); Hilbert, Grundlagen der Geometrie (1899); Hartshorne, Geometry:
// Euclid and Beyond (2000); Coxeter, Projective Geometry (2nd ed. 1974); Artin, Geometric Algebra (1957); Schneider,
// Convex Bodies: The Brunn–Minkowski Theory (2nd ed. 2014); do Carmo, Differential Geometry of Curves and Surfaces
// (1976) and Riemannian Geometry (1992); Lee, Introduction to Riemannian Manifolds (2nd ed. 2018); McDuff and Salamon,
// Introduction to Symplectic Topology (3rd ed. 2017). Not checked by a specialist.
// Checked by ../../tests/check-theorems.js.

